\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord, while for all mankind we pray,
\par Of every clime and coast, 
\par Or hear us for our native land,
\par The land we love the most.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Our fathers' sepulchres are here,
\par And here our kindred dwell,
\par Our children too: how should we love
\par Another land so dwell?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O guard our shores from every foe
\par With peace our bothers bless:
\par With prosperous times our cities crown,
\par Our fields with plenteousness.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Unite us in the sacred love
\par Of knowledge, truth, and Thee;
\par And let our hills and valleys shout
\par The songs of liberty.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Lord of the nations, thus to Thee
\par Our country we commend;
\par Be Thou her refuge and her trust,
\par Her everlasting friend.
\par Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

